  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Reverse Pipe Problems and Unknown Times",
    "description": "Recover individual pipe times from together-times, ratios, differences, and pairwise information.",
    "teachingApproach": "Build rate equations from the story rather than guessing times. Start with one known individual time, then fixed time differences, time ratios, pairwise rates, and quadratic capacity questions. Whenever a quadratic gives two roots, keep only the positive physically meaningful time or flow rate.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 32,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 16, Pipes and Cisterns. Approved scope: Teach reverse-rate algebra. Cover one known pipe plus a together-time, individual times differing by a fixed number of hours, one pipe being a multiple of another, pairwise rates, and questions where the unknown appears in a reciprocal equation that becomes quadratic. Use positive-time checks to reject impossible roots. Include a pump whose fill and empty capacities differ by a fixed rate and whose times differ by a fixed amount. Learners should form rate equations from the story rather than guess times."
  },
